WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
So, now let's talk about skills. And

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.550
skills, I would say, are the most useful

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.670
things in CloudCode. It's the one

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.350
feature that I use daily, and in my

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.790
view, it is also the fastest way for you

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.470
to feel the power of these agentic

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.510
coding platforms. And before I show you

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.750
some of these skills in action, first

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.510
let's define what a skill is, because

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.430
it's really rather simple. Because a

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.470
skill, you can think of it as a recipe

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.670
card that your agent keeps. It is a

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.750
written document that when your agent

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.390
needs to do a job, it follows the

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.710
instructions on that specific card. And

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.390
like I mentioned, what it looks like is

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.230
it's simply just a text file,

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.790
specifically a markdown file. So, it has

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.550
a description here at the top, and then

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.710
it has the body section here that just

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.790
provides it instructions on what to do

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.430
whenever this skill is invoked. For

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.790
example, these slides that you're

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.950
seeing, these are all created by this

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.310
/robo skill that I created. So, if you

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.390
dive into our IDE now, you can see here

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.630
that skills, by default, they live in

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.110
this folder called .cloud. So, whenever

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.470
you create a skill, which I'll show you

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.790
how to do that in just a bit, by

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.430
default, CloudCode will create them

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.110
within this folder. And from within this

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.070
folder, you can see that I have several

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.750
skills in here, which none of them I

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.270
wrote myself. All of them have been

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.470
created by my agent. And if we look at

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.590
this folder called robo, under this

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.390
skill.md, the contents of that, that is

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.110
basically the recipe card that I was

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.350
talking about. So, each skill has this

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.190
section at the top that gives it its

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.030
name, as well as a description. So, you

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.750
can see here, if you hover over it, it

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.710
says that the description of the skill

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.470
is added to every request and will be

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.790
used by the agent to decide when to load

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.710
the skill. And then you have the body

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.910
section, which is not automatically

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.950
loaded within your session, but will be

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.390
loaded whenever this skill is invoked.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.070
And you can see this is quite a long

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.830
skill, because this is meant for design.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.110
It is dialed in to the slides that I was

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.830
making earlier. And just to show you how

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.310
my CloudCode has some knowledge already

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.110
of the skills that I have in my

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.910
workspace, you can actually test it and

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.510
give it this prompt where I'm asking it

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.790
to show me the skills already preloaded

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.430
in this session, which is a raw new

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.550
session, and the exact text that is

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.230
preloaded. And you can see for my

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.270
workspace, if I send that, it gives me a

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.510
view of some of the memory files that is

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.469
truly preloaded, meaning the whole text

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:11.990
is included in the session, which we

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.430
will talk more about in the memory

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.470
modules. But you can see here in number

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.110
two that it is already listing, but not

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.830
really preloading the whole body of the

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.510
180 skills that I have in my workspace.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.350
And these 180 skills, you can see that

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.590
it's telling us that it can see right

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.150
now each one's name plus description

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.910
plus the trigger phrases and nothing

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.110
more. So going back to that skill.md,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.070
essentially what is already preloaded in

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.750
every chat that you begin with Claude

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.910
Code is the name of the skill, the

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.670
description, and also these triggers.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.430
And it preloads only this small snippet

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.390
across all of the skills that I have

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.030
here. And so you can see if I ask it to

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.230
give us the one that you're seeing

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.230
currently for /robo, the skill that we

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.750
were just viewing, it's telling us that

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.470
it is currently seeing the name of that

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.270
skill as well as that description that

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.509
we just saw in the skill.md. And so in

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:01.150
order to use the skill, there's actually

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.509
multiple ways by which you can invoke

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:05.229
it. So if you just say the skill's name

00:03:05.239 --> 00:03:06.910
like run the robo skill, because that

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.710
whole description of the skill is

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.430
already preloaded in your chat, then

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.430
your agent will recognize what skill

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.870
you're talking about. If you want to

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.390
invoke it directly, you can type in /

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.949
and then the name of the skill, or

00:03:17.959 --> 00:03:19.310
depending on the job that you're after,

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.229
you can actually just let Claude pick it

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:23.470
out for you. So to give a quick example,

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.830
if I type in /, you can see all of the

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.750
different commands that I have in here,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.390
including my skills plus the ones that

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.550
come in default with Claude Code. But if

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.710
I type in robo, that will invoke the

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.509
skill directly, and I can just say my

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:37.110
prompt here where I'm saying that I want

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.190
to create a sample one slider, to say hi

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.949
to the viewer of this course. And what

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:43.190
it will do essentially is it will look

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.070
for that skill, it'll read the skill.md

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.430
file, and inject this whole context,

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.630
this whole text file, into that session

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.509
so that it has proper knowledge of the

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:54.030
design system that we built for these

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.910
slides. And then it will build out the

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.670
slide just like we ask. And once it's

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.150
finished, you can see it created this

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.110
slide with the font that we assigned to

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.790
it, that dot matrix design that we have

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.870
in the skill, and essentially all of the

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.790
colors and the font styling, plus the

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.790
visuals that we assigned to make this

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.240
whole design system skill.
